  "note": "Collectible palettes (book/scripts/modules/collection.mjs; canon .spw/surfaces/collecting.spw). Each is named for a place, mixed by hand from the maker's own description of a laminated folio (or, where no folio fits yet, from the chapter's own plate) (spwashi.com, where the folio lives and is linked from here; lore.land never copies or claims it). A palette carries its colour (ground, ink, accent, glow, edge) and its type (the lettering the folio wears, projected onto the four type roles the site has: display serif, body serif, mono, and case/tracking/style). A chapter's palette is earned by finishing that chapter in any dimension (reading to its end, carrying the pie through it, keeping its own wonders) and, once earned, the chapter wears it: headings, drop caps, rules and a faint wash take its colours, and its headings its type. The mime wash is earned by winning a chapter back from Mimes Against WAP. Spw atom: =palette[id].",
